#!/bin/sh
# Switch the micro-USB port between device mode (PC link, charging) and host
# mode (keyboard, mouse, USB stick). This board cannot supply 5 V to the port,
# so host mode only works through a powered OTG Y-cable or a powered hub.
# Usage: usb-host-mode [host|device|toggle]
R=$(ls -d /sys/class/usb_role/*/role 2>/dev/null | head -1)
if [ -z "$R" ]; then
	notify-send -i drive-removable-media "USB" "No USB role switch (kernel without OTG)"
	exit 1
fi

case "${1:-toggle}" in
host|device) new=$1 ;;
*) if [ "$(cat "$R")" = host ]; then new=device; else new=host; fi ;;
esac

if echo "$new" > "$R"; then
	if [ "$new" = host ]; then
		msg="Host mode: use a powered OTG cable or hub"
	else
		msg="Device mode: PC connection and charging"
	fi
	notify-send -i drive-removable-media "USB" "$msg"
else
	notify-send -i drive-removable-media "USB" "Could not switch to $new"
	exit 1
fi
